  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yvy Temity Nhagareko: Guarani way of caring for the Land</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Guarani Indigenous people in Southern Brazil face food insecurity caused by limited access to land and income-generating opportunities. The IAF supports community-led solutions for expanding food security and economic inclusion for historically marginalized groups. IAF grantee Associao Tembi?u Por (ATP ) will support Guarani families in developing agroforestry systems for food production in the Indigenous territory of Rio das Cobras in western Paran state, to improve their food security and foster a healthier diet. ATP is also investing in a processing facility for surplus fruits and vegetables with aims to supply local schools with healthy foods. This grant is part of a cohort of Indigenous organizations based across Brazil that aim to support their communities and promote spaces for exchange and learning among different ethnicities facing complex challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
